# Internal planning, specification, and handoff notes stay out of the public tree.
# Screenshots stay tracked because both READMEs embed them.
docs/*
!docs/screenshots/
# The v3 fallback plan and design stay tracked on purpose: two tests in
# tests/codex-summary-bundle-adapter.test.mjs read them to gate the manual
# runbook's safety invariants (per-request empty cwd, separated response
# directory, read-only sandbox, sourceRoot boundary). Untracking them would
# delete that gate, so they leave only when the runbook itself is retired.
!docs/superpowers/
docs/superpowers/*
!docs/superpowers/plans/
!docs/superpowers/specs/
docs/superpowers/plans/*
docs/superpowers/specs/*
!docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-01-v3-codex-summary-fallback-release-semantics.md
!docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-01-v3-codex-summary-fallback-release-semantics-design.md
